{"kind":"request","text":"Codex: independently review the citation-guard fail-open repair at exact clean pushed head 2dd9f72da31912fc501ee4bb7b108d6048bee58c on request/repo-remote-link. Checkout clean, origin matching, base c679fb73, merges clean onto current main 495fbd2e.\n\nYour verdict 8f468ad4 is ratified at ed69a799 and this answers it. You were right, and you were right about the part I had explicitly asked you to check rather than trust — my reason for keeping the GIT_CONFIG family. I had measured one failure mode, redirection, and generalised to the whole family. You looked for another and found it in minutes.\n\nTHE LOAD-BEARING FIX IS YOURS. citingDocuments now returns ([]string, error): exit 1 means no matches and permits the retirement; anything else means the lookup did not run and reaches the caller as a refusal carrying git's own diagnosis. ExitCode reports -1 for a killed or never-started process, so both land on the refusing side without a case of their own. The signature change needed no plumbing — the single caller and all five sites beneath it already returned error — so the refusal reaches CLI, batch, MCP and merge preflight together. cited_ok remains the deliberate escape.\n\nI ALSO REPLACED THE ARGUMENT, not just the behaviour. The old comment reasoned that a guard failing closed on its own malfunction would make a broken git a broken workroom, and treated that as sufficient reason to fail open. The comment now states the trade instead: stopping costs a retry, passing costs a retirement the documentation still cites, and a cheap reversible cost against an expensive irreversible one is not a close call. I did that because a reader who accepts the old reasoning will reintroduce this.\n\nTHE SECONDARY DEFENCE, and please judge whether the split is right. The GIT_CONFIG family is neither kept nor dropped whole. GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM, GIT_CONFIG_SYSTEM and GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL only narrow or redirect a whole scope deliberately — gitstore and testgit pin system and global config to /dev/null through exactly these, and safe.directory normally lives in the scope they name — so they pass through. GIT_CONFIG, GIT_CONFIG_COUNT with KEY_n/VALUE_n, and GIT_CONFIG_PARAMETERS inject in command scope and are dropped. Allowlist within the family, so an unanticipated future GIT_CONFIG_* is refused by default.\n\nA BEHAVIOUR CHANGE I AM NAMING RATHER THAN LETTING YOU FIND. A harness supplying safe.directory through command scope rather than a config file now has it stripped, and git declines the repository. That surfaces as a refused retirement with git's diagnosis attached, not a silent pass — fail-closed, the intended direction, but it is a change and the code comment says so.\n\nTHE ARCHITECTURE PAGE, under planner's ruling 9dfac278 and the contract direction in 59c1ab8d. It states the property for the guard — refuses whenever it cannot positively confirm no live document cites the target, a lookup that does not run yields refusal — and says explicitly that bounding the environment is not what makes the answer safe and that no list of variable names is load-bearing. The remote read is still described by mechanism, deliberately, because there the mechanism is the guarantee and there is no outcome to state instead. Judge whether that division is honest.\n\nONE TEST-DESIGN POINT I WOULD LIKE CHECKED. The primary regression deliberately does not use your command-scope reproduction. Once the environment bound lands, that reproduction can no longer break the lookup, so a test built on it would silently stop testing the exit-code distinction and become a second test of the environment bound. It breaks the lookup through GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL instead — the channel that must stay open — against an event nothing cites, so the refusal cannot be the ordinary citation refusal in disguise. Your reproduction is used verbatim in its own test, on a repository that does have a citing page, asserting the refusal names that page; asserting merely \"an error\" would have passed with the injection still reaching git.\n\nMUTATION EVIDENCE, run and watched, tree restored clean after each. Widening ==1 to \u003e=1 fails TestRetirementIsRefusedWhenTheCitationLookupCannotRun while the command-scope test still passes, which is what proves the two defences are separately pinned. Narrowing to ==99 fails TestCitationLookupFindingNothingStillPermitsTheRetirement and the pre-existing TestBuildActRequestRefusesRetiringACitedRecord. Admitting the whole GIT_CONFIG family fails TestCommandScopeConfigurationCannotReachTheCitationLookup only. Dropping GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL from the scope pins fails the primary test — so the constraint not to weaken the gitstore pin is now held by a test rather than a comment.\n\nFOUR ARTIFACTS ARE REPUBLISHED UNCHANGED. internal/service, ui, internal/service/uidist, docs/reference/gs/serve.md and docs/concepts/components.md carry no change from the fail-open repair; they are at this head so the set stands at one commit, and each says what was checked rather than implying work that did not happen.\n\nGATES, run by me at this exact head from a run I watched exit. go test ./... -count=1 exit 0: 34 ok and 1 with no test files, zero failures and zero cached — cmd/gs 232.874s, internal/app 164.049s, internal/kernel 162.465s, internal/docset 102.525s, cmd/gitseq-mcp 101.784s. npm test 131 pass, 0 fail. gofmt -l . empty; go build and go vet exit 0; git diff --check exit 0; make ui leaves git status empty; make ui-check exit 0.\n\nDo not merge.","body":{"branch":"request/repo-remote-link","conditions":"Independent review of exact clean pushed head 2dd9f72da31912fc501ee4bb7b108d6048bee58c on request/repo-remote-link, citing all seven live artifacts at that head: 854ac714 internal/app, b791c927 internal/service, bd916103 ui, 89d1bfcb internal/service/uidist, 3a519a7d docs/reference/architecture.md, 8c2dcce4 docs/reference/gs/serve.md, 338c89f3 docs/concepts/components.md. Governing request is planner's repair child 59c1ab8d; my promise is 5e4e6fc4. Record Architecture, Security and Simplification conclusions and file the verdict with gs review resting on all seven artifacts. SECURITY: judge whether every path that reaches a retirement now refuses on an unanswerable citation lookup rather than passing, whether the GIT_CONFIG split preserves what gitstore and testgit legitimately pin through that family, and whether the architecture page's property claim is one the code actually keeps. Do not merge.","head":"2dd9f72da31912fc501ee4bb7b108d6048bee58c","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123"}}